To install **Helm 3** on Ubuntu, follow these steps.

## Method 1: Install Helm using the Official Script (Recommended)

### Step 1: Update the package index

```bash
sudo apt update
```

### Step 2: Download the Helm installation script

```bash
curl -fsSL -o get_helm.sh https://raw.githubusercontent.com/helm/helm/main/scripts/get-helm-3
```

### Step 3: Give execute permission

```bash
chmod 700 get_helm.sh
```

### Step 4: Run the script

```bash
sudo ./get_helm.sh
```

### Step 5: Verify the installation

```bash
helm version
```

Example output:

```bash
version.BuildInfo{Version:"v3.19.0", GitCommit:"...", GoVersion:"go1.24.x"}
```

---

# Method 2: Install using the Helm APT Repository

### Step 1: Update packages

```bash
sudo apt update
```

### Step 2: Install required packages

```bash
sudo apt install curl gpg apt-transport-https --yes
```

### Step 3: Download the Helm GPG key

```bash
curl https://baltocdn.com/helm/signing.asc | gpg --dearmor | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/helm.gpg > /dev/null
```

### Step 4: Add the Helm repository

```bash
echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/helm.gpg] https://baltocdn.com/helm/stable/debian/ all main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/helm-stable-debian.list
```

### Step 5: Update package list

```bash
sudo apt update
```

### Step 6: Install Helm

```bash
sudo apt install helm -y
```

### Step 7: Verify installation

```bash
helm version
```

